\f1\b\fs24 \cf2 How to use:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
Put this script in your iTunes Scripts folder. This is located in 
\f2\i \cf3 user name
\f0\i0  > Library > iTunes\cf0 . If there is no folder named "Scripts" there, create one and put the script in it. It will then appear in iTunes' Script menu, where you can activate it by clicking on its name.\
\
You can run the script by selecting it from iTunes' Script menu. Or, you can double-click on its icon in the Finder.\
\
\'a5 You will be asked if you want to search your designated "Music" folder or to choose another folder containing audio files. The designated "Music" folder is the one set in iTunes' Advanced Preferences. Any other folder selected will have its complete contents searched for audio files, no matter how deep they may be. So, you 
\f2\i could
\f0\i0  select an entire drive.\
\
\'a5 You will be asked if you want Spotlight to re-index the selected folder. This will take a little extra time.\
\
In a few moments a text file will be created in your Desktop folder listing the file paths of the audio files in the selected folder. The file paths will be sorted alphabetically.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

\fs36 \cf0 \
